"2025-09-17T09:45:00\",\"md5\":\"a80f0ad4af9fd250a462680c85e6fbf0\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\\\\3u84xhcdicdb6vqtlfud7syhj444z2.txt\",\"previewPath\":\"c:\\\\users\\\\xiaoxinpro 16 iah\\\\documents\\\\qtcore\\\\pdffile\\\\4bb6e885c6b375f7991ed237ae550f5a.pdf\",\"priority\":3,\"score\":0.0,\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"tokenNum\":414,\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"createTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:56:32.666\",\"description\":\"Archie receives orders to join the earl and a large group of soldiers in pursuit of Bruce after a traitor reveals Bruce’s recent whereabouts. Despite his reluctance, Archie prepares to lead the party using Hector, the hound, whose tracking skills are crucial for the search. Archie contemplates killing the hound and fleeing if they get close to Bruce, though escape seems unlikely given the number of mounted men. Guided by a local peasant, the group reaches a cottage five miles away where Hector becomes highly excited, thoroughly investigating the area before decisively taking up Bruce’s trail. Archie struggles to control the eager hound, who pulls hard on the chain. He cautions Pembroke, the earl, to keep the knights and soldiers at a distance, noting that their noise further agitates Hector and makes the dog harder to manage. The narrative details the tension and urgency of the pursuit, highlighting Archie’s internal conflict and the hound’s pivotal role.\",\"docName\":\"3z3zlgnnsiuha76yy56h6uu71bh3q1\",\"editTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:57:41.133\",\"fileName\":\"3z3zlgnnsiuha76yy56h6uu71bh3q1.txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\",\"id\":1987776371266555904,\"isDeleted\":0,\"isTmpFile\":false,\"labelNameList\":[\"History\",\"Report\",\"Text Document\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-09-17T09:45:00\",\"md5\":\"bb28043dd606535bdcaf1ee30346b0f9\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\\\\3z3zlgnnsiuha76yy56h6uu71bh3q1.txt\",\"previewPath\":\"c:\\\\users\\\\xiaoxinpro 16 iah\\\\documents\\\\qtcore\\\\pdffile\\\\e6e2343232ca421ef2da852a5f84548c.pdf\",\"priority\":4,\"score\":0.0,\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"tokenNum\":326,\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"createTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:56:32.695\",\"description\":\"This document outlines the design method for evaluating AI face algorithms, focusing on test set collection and variable matrices. Key variables include head movements (pitch, yaw, roll), facial motions (mouth, eyebrow, eyelid), and lighting conditions (weak, medium, strong, uneven). Motion transfers involve horizontal and angular head movements, while expression transfers and optical flow are assessed under varied light environments. The evaluation uses only laptop cameras, with tools from Ruifeng for video input/output collection. Collection involves preparing 70 videos, at least 5 seconds each, covering head and facial movement variables and lighting conditions, with 10 videos per variable. Each variable should ideally have data from multiple participants, covering at least 7 individuals. Driving videos and output videos are compared to assess algorithm performance, using selected source images and ground truth from videos.\",\"docName\":\"AI_Face_Test_Set_Collection_Method_Design\",\"editTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:57:50.923\",\"fileName\":\"AI_Face_Test_Set_Collection_Method_Design.pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\",\"id\":1987776371388190720,\"isDeleted\":0,\"isTmpFile\":false,\"labelNameList\":[\"Technology\",\"Data Analysis\",\"Specifications\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-09-17T09:46:00\",\"md5\":\"b0f396e7936e0f6192cd880927e8e74b\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\\\\AI_Face_Test_Set_Collection_Method_Design.pptx\",\"previewPath\":\"c:\\\\users\\\\xiaoxinpro 16 iah\\\\documents\\\\qtcore\\\\pdffile\\\\5820f6ff633a3666eab35d871b69006b.pdf\",\"priority\":5,\"score\":0.0,\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"tokenNum\":432,\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"createTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:56:32.726\",\"description\":\"This document provides an introduction to Linear Programming (LP), detailing its definition, historical development, solution methods, and strategies for testing LP solvers. LP focuses on optimizing a linear objective function subject to linear constraints, with solutions within a convex polyhedral feasible set. Mixed-Integer Programming (MIP) extends LP by allowing some variables to be integers, solved using techniques like Branch-and-Bound. The history covers key contributors: G.B. Dantzig (concept, Simplex Method), L.V. Kantorovich and T.C. Koopmans (Nobel Prize), L.G. Khachian (Ellipsoid Method), and N. Karmarkar (Interior-Point Method). Solution methods include enumeration, the Simplex Method (effective in practice but exponential in worst cases), and the Interior-Point Method (polynomial-time efficiency for large problems). LP solvers are tested using both benchmark and self-built test sets, including classic optimization models with varying size and structure. Testing approaches include handling unique, infinite, infeasible, and unbounded problems, using different coefficient scales and constraints to evaluate solver robustness and correctness.\",\"docName\":\"A_brief_introduction_of_LP_liutao21_20220615\",\"editTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:58:06.320\",\"fileName\":\"A_brief_introduction_of_LP_liutao21_20220615.pptx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\",\"id\":1987776371518214144,\"isDeleted\":0,\"isTmpFile\":false,\"labelNameList\":[\"Technology\",\"Specifications\",\"Training\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-09-17T09:46:00\",\"md5\":\"0dbb2532524843af54fb3388b7bf3381\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\\\\A_brief_introduction_of_LP_liutao21_20220615.pptx\",\"previewPath\":\"c:\\\\users\\\\xiaoxinpro 16 iah\\\\documents\\\\qtcore\\\\pdffile\\\\d590d120fc4bcc9bc01d308c3ad03c90.pdf\",\"priority\":6,\"score\":0.0,\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"tokenNum\":1297,\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"createTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:56:32.800\",\"description\":\"This document provides an overview of Belfast English, its origins, and sociolinguistic investigations into language variation across different social networks in Belfast. Founded in 1603, Belfast grew rapidly in the 19th century due to industrialisation and migration following the Great Famine. The city's English evolved as an amalgamation of linguistic features from western Scotland, northern England, and unique local traits. Key sociolinguistic studies, particularly by James and Lesley Milroy, examined how language use in Belfast is influenced by social networks—ties within neighbourhoods that vary in density and multiplexity. Strong, dense networks (often working-class, with high solidarity) resist external linguistic norms, while loose networks (middle-class, status-oriented) tend to adopt standard speech. Detailed investigations were conducted in three areas: Ballymacarrett, Hammer, and Clonard, revealing differences in phonological variables (such as palatalisation, dental realisations, and vowel raising) that correlate with community structure, gender, and age. The Milroys highlighted the role of local linguistic norms in shaping identity and excluding outsiders, noting that vernacular speech retains unique markers not easily acquired by non-natives. Their research contributed to broader linguistic theory, illustrating the variation and rules within vernacular communities versus the standardized norms. The document is supported by a comprehensive set of academic references related to Belfast English and sociolinguistic research.\",\"docName\":\"Belfast-English\",\"editTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:58:22.145\",\"fileName\":\"Belfast-English.docx\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\",\"id\":1987776371828592640,\"isDeleted\":0,\"isTmpFile\":false,\"labelNameList\":[\"History\",\"Data Analysis\",\"Research Paper\"],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-09-17T09:45:00\",\"md5\":\"3193e699ffa92db332ae31a9fb1d3cb4\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\\\\Belfast-English.docx\",\"previewPath\":\"c:\\\\users\\\\xiaoxinpro 16 iah\\\\documents\\\\qtcore\\\\pdffile\\\\7d62eed3de32f05711820c16bc2bd670.pdf\",\"priority\":7,\"score\":0.0,\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"tokenNum\":2989,\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"createTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:56:32.823\",\"description\":\"\",\"docName\":\"\",\"editTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:58:17.612\",\"fileName\":\"British-Food-Culture.doc\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\",\"id\":1987776371925061632,\"isDeleted\":0,\"isTmpFile\":false,\"labelNameList\":[],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-09-17T09:45:00\",\"md5\":\"435798f1c3377c7f5b71e18d733ca579\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\\\\British-Food-Culture.doc\",\"priority\":8,\"score\":0.0,\"status\":\"RUNNING\",\"tokenNum\":0,\"uriPath\":\"\"},{\"createTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:56:32.847\",\"description\":\"\",\"docName\":\"\",\"editTime\":\"2025-11-10T14:56:32.847\",\"errorDescription\":\"\",\"fileName\":\"Netflix Becomes a Broadway Producer With Peter Morgan’s Patriots.txt\",\"folder\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\",\"id\":1987776372025724928,\"isDeleted\":0,\"isTmpFile\":false,\"labelNameList\":[],\"lastModifyTime\":\"2025-09-17T09:46:00\",\"md5\":\"ab84c46eaa62a18048fb0241446da4ca\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\XiaoXinPro 16 IAH\\\\Desktop\\\\LRIA_llm_eval\\\\eval\\\\Quantum_e2e_v20251106\\\\Bvt1110\\\\bvtfiles\\\\Netflix Becomes a Broadway Producer With Peter Morgan’s Patriots.txt\",\"priority\":9,\"score\":0.0,\"status\":\"ADDED\",\"tokenNum\":0,\"uriPath\":\"\"}]"}}
